       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Overdoses of this size can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo. Usual dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily. Use 2.5 mg for frail or elderly patients, or for patients with hepatic impairment.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your resident or attending. Once you've confirmed it, for example 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, I'll enter the order right away. If you do want 50 mg for an unusual reason, it will need explicit sign-off from the supervising physician, and I'd want that documented in the order note."
      }
